WEBVTT

00:00:01.283 --> 00:00:02.450
[PHOENIX] Turns out I have
an imposter who earned

00:00:02.533 --> 00:00:04.825
a guilty plea for
a client of mine.

00:00:04.908 --> 00:00:06.908
I can't let injustice
happen on my watch,

00:00:06.991 --> 00:00:10.241
so I petitioned for a retrial
to prove her innocence.

00:00:10.325 --> 00:00:12.658
But the testimonies
given by the two star witnesses

00:00:12.741 --> 00:00:14.616
left a bad taste in my mouth.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.241
Something is definitely
rotten here.

00:00:17.325 --> 00:00:19.283
Maggey swears
she saw the killer.

00:00:19.366 --> 00:00:20.866
But where did they go?

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.408
To get to the bottom of this,

00:00:22.491 --> 00:00:25.283
I'm returning to the scene of
the crime to look for clues.

00:00:28.241 --> 00:00:29.950
[MAYA]
Bonjour, Monsieur!

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.158
[PHOENIX]
Maya?

00:00:34.241 --> 00:00:36.575
That's moi! Très Bien!

00:02:08.408 --> 00:02:10.616
[MAYA] That retrial really
made things more complicated,

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:12.491
don't you think?

00:02:12.575 --> 00:02:13.950
It's true,
we definitely have a lot

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.658
on out plate in this case.

00:02:15.741 --> 00:02:17.158
The elusive second waitress,

00:02:17.241 --> 00:02:19.533
and the victim's
mysterious earpiece.

00:02:19.616 --> 00:02:20.700
It's strange.

00:02:20.783 --> 00:02:22.075
And then there's
that whole imposter thing

00:02:22.158 --> 00:02:23.658
with Fake-nix Wrong

00:02:23.741 --> 00:02:26.366
I'm not sure I can
stomach that part of it.

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:28.825
By the way...
Is he the only customer?

00:02:28.908 --> 00:02:30.700
Yeah, this place is so boring.

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:32.866
You should order something
to liven things up!

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:34.075
It is lunchtime.

00:02:34.158 --> 00:02:35.700
So I think you should
get today's special,

00:02:35.783 --> 00:02:37.241
which is the Twin-T plate!

00:02:37.325 --> 00:02:40.075
Twin-T, eh?
Well, how much is that?

00:02:40.158 --> 00:02:42.283
That'll be 20,
thank you kindly!

00:02:42.366 --> 00:02:44.158
--No way!
--Aw, come on, Nick!

00:02:44.241 --> 00:02:45.533
Be a sport and get it, please!

00:02:45.616 --> 00:02:47.908
No, honestly, this
case has killed my appetite.

00:02:47.991 --> 00:02:49.658
Well, this will bring it back!

00:02:49.741 --> 00:02:53.241
One special coming up!
Twin-T, see-voo-play!

00:02:53.325 --> 00:02:54.950
Hey, wait a second, Maya!

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.616
[MAYA] Here. Bone-apple-teeth
to you, mon-sewer.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:02:59.908
Wow, this actually
looks like it could be

00:02:59.991 --> 00:03:01.283
worth 20 bucks.

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:04.533
[PHOENIX groans]

00:03:04.616 --> 00:03:06.075
Y'okay?

00:03:06.908 --> 00:03:08.616
I think my tongue hates me now.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:11.950
[MAYA] Oh. That explains
why this place is so empty.

00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:13.866
[GUMSHOE]
Yeah, that's the number, pal!

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:15.741
Come on, come on, come on!

00:03:15.825 --> 00:03:17.950
Now give me an eight!
I can smell it coming up!

00:03:18.033 --> 00:03:18.950
I know that voice.

00:03:19.033 --> 00:03:20.950
[yells]
No! I said an eight!

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:22.950
[yells

00:03:23.033 --> 00:03:23.950
Hello?

00:03:24.033 --> 00:03:24.950
[GUMSHOE]
Huh?

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:27.116
[gasps]

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:29.658
A little radio? Ah, I get it.

00:03:29.741 --> 00:03:31.408
What exactly do you get, bub?

00:03:31.491 --> 00:03:32.658
Well, from what I overheard,

00:03:32.741 --> 00:03:34.366
it sounded to me like
you were listening to

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:35.950
the lottery results just now.

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:37.325
[GUMSHOE growls]

00:03:37.408 --> 00:03:38.825
[PHOENIX] Knowing how
Glen Elg hit the big jackpot

00:03:38.908 --> 00:03:41.741
right before he kicked the
bucket gave you an idea. Right?

00:03:41.825 --> 00:03:44.366
Are you some kind of psychic
mind reader or something?

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.200
No, it was just really obvious.

00:03:46.283 --> 00:03:47.616
You got me, kid.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.783
I was listening to "Millionaire
Radio" where they read

00:03:49.866 --> 00:03:53.033
the results, and I guess I kinda
let myself get carried away.

00:03:53.116 --> 00:03:55.741
Millionaire, huh?
I could see listening to that.

00:03:55.825 --> 00:03:57.408
[GUMSHOE] It comes
on Wednesdays at 1:30

00:03:57.491 --> 00:04:01.491
and runs for about ten minutes,
if you wanna check it out.

00:04:01.575 --> 00:04:03.116
I'll buy a ticket today!

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.491
Good luck!

00:04:04.575 --> 00:04:05.741
By the way...

00:04:05.825 --> 00:04:08.325
Maggey didn't happen to
say anything, did she?

00:04:08.408 --> 00:04:10.408
I don't recall her
saying anything, do you?

00:04:10.491 --> 00:04:13.408
No, no. Not really.

00:04:13.491 --> 00:04:15.241
Just tell me what
she said about me.

00:04:15.325 --> 00:04:16.658
I can take it.

00:04:16.741 --> 00:04:18.450
To be honest, we all
know you painted her

00:04:18.533 --> 00:04:21.408
into a corner with the
testimony you gave the court.

00:04:21.491 --> 00:04:22.825
So, after the trial...

00:04:22.908 --> 00:04:25.200
I can hardly believe
that stupid ol' Dick!

00:04:25.283 --> 00:04:27.116
Ugh! I hate him!

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.075
[yells]

00:04:29.158 --> 00:04:31.533
What could I do?

00:04:31.616 --> 00:04:32.825
Take it easy.

00:04:32.908 --> 00:04:33.991
These things happen, pal.

00:04:34.075 --> 00:04:35.616
You ain't helpin' me here, doll.

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:36.991
So, uh...

00:04:37.075 --> 00:04:38.950
I assume the reason you came
here today was because

00:04:39.033 --> 00:04:41.116
you wanted to question
Mr. Armstrong again.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.783
Yeah. That's the chef!

00:04:42.866 --> 00:04:45.200
Well, coincidentally,
that's why I'm here, too.

00:04:45.283 --> 00:04:48.366
Oh, he's back in the kitchen.

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:51.491
Weird. I could swear
he was just here.

00:04:51.575 --> 00:04:54.283
[MAYA] A vanity? I guess
he does his makeup here?

00:04:54.366 --> 00:04:55.825
[PHOENIX]
What's all this?

00:04:55.908 --> 00:04:57.741
[GUMSHOE]
Looks like aromatherapy bottles.

00:04:57.825 --> 00:05:00.450
[PHOENIX] Okay. But one of these
things is not like the others.

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:03.408
Yeah, you're right.
Doesn't even have a label.

00:05:03.491 --> 00:05:05.116
[GUMSHOE]
A mystery liquid?

00:05:07.408 --> 00:05:08.533
It's odorless.

00:05:08.616 --> 00:05:11.325
But I'll tell you what,
I smell a rat here!

00:05:12.616 --> 00:05:15.033
I'm gonna take this
back to the boys in the lab.

00:05:15.116 --> 00:05:17.116
Get Byrde outta that cage!

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:21.325
See ya, pal.

00:05:22.325 --> 00:05:25.991
[ARMSTRONG]
Oui-oui. Next month?

00:05:26.075 --> 00:05:28.408
[VIOLA]
If you don't have it by then,

00:05:28.491 --> 00:05:31.366
I'll turn your
bistro into toast.

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:32.366
[giggles]

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:35.991
[screams]
That won't be necessary!

00:05:36.075 --> 00:05:38.033
[VIOLA]
Don't let me down.

00:05:38.116 --> 00:05:40.616
Because I'll be watching you
like a hawk, doughboy.

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:41.991
[giggles]

00:05:42.075 --> 00:05:43.408
[PHOENIX]
That's her.

00:05:44.783 --> 00:05:46.241
Au revoir!

00:05:47.783 --> 00:05:50.116
[sighs]
Ooh-la-la!

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:51.491
[MAYA whimpers]

00:05:51.575 --> 00:05:53.158
Sorry.

00:05:53.241 --> 00:05:56.033
[ARMSTRONG]
Non. Zis is who I am.

00:05:56.116 --> 00:05:59.491
I try to be un petite angel,
but my wings, zay are broken.

00:05:59.575 --> 00:06:01.700
I 'ave to do everyzing
'e tells me to.

00:06:01.783 --> 00:06:04.075
I'm at ze mercy of
the Big City Tiger!

00:06:04.158 --> 00:06:05.241
Big City Tiger?

00:06:05.325 --> 00:06:06.616
You must be very
careful when you need

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:08.825
to borrow a few francs
from someone, no?

00:06:08.908 --> 00:06:10.366
Every time 'e
starts to yell and rage

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:14.033
with z'at spiky head
of 'is... si terrifiant!

00:06:14.116 --> 00:06:15.325
Oh! 'E will flatten me

00:06:15.408 --> 00:06:17.325
like a crepe
and use me as a rug!

00:06:17.408 --> 00:06:20.158
[BOTH]
Like a crepe?

00:06:20.241 --> 00:06:22.283
[MAYA]
The Big City Tiger sounds scary.

00:06:22.366 --> 00:06:24.408
You sure you can
just leave the restaurant?

00:06:24.491 --> 00:06:26.616
[MAYA] Yeah. I'm on
break until dinner time.

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:30.325
[KUDO] Hey! You think
you're too good for my seeds?

00:06:30.408 --> 00:06:32.741
Ya lousy buncha ingrates!

00:06:35.533 --> 00:06:37.825
[MAYA]
What a kooky guy!

00:06:37.908 --> 00:06:38.866
[PHOENIX]
Hello!

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:41.450
Argh. And now you! Hmph!

00:06:41.533 --> 00:06:44.033
I hope you can forgive
me about what happened in court.

00:06:44.116 --> 00:06:46.241
Well. You weren't
wrong, were ya, Wright?

00:06:46.325 --> 00:06:48.158
I was so busy admiring
the waitress's figure,

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:49.741
that I didn't see her face.

00:06:49.825 --> 00:06:51.283
I'm just a dirty old man!

00:06:51.366 --> 00:06:53.491
Buh-buh-birdie!
Pretty, pretty bird!

00:06:53.575 --> 00:06:56.783
Okay, then.
Work your magic, Maya.

00:06:56.866 --> 00:06:59.991
Hey, sir. What do you say you
and I have a teeny little chat?

00:07:00.075 --> 00:07:01.741
With a "teeny little" girl?

00:07:01.825 --> 00:07:05.366
No, thank you.
Run along and play on the slide.

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:06.366
Ow!

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:07.491
[PHOENIX]
Didn't take the bait.

00:07:07.575 --> 00:07:10.033
[MIA]
Excuse me. Do you have a moment?

00:07:10.116 --> 00:07:11.116
Huh?

00:07:13.075 --> 00:07:15.033
Have all the time
you want missy!

00:07:15.116 --> 00:07:16.700
[PHOENIX]
Mia?

00:07:16.783 --> 00:07:18.491
Good. Thank you.

00:07:18.575 --> 00:07:20.991
I hope you don't mind talking
to me for a few minutes.

00:07:21.075 --> 00:07:24.825
Sure. I'm Victor Kudo,
nice to meet ya.

00:07:24.908 --> 00:07:27.450
That trial must've
been so hard on you.

00:07:27.533 --> 00:07:28.866
You bet yer tookis.

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:31.116
No matter what anyone says,
I know what I saw!

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.700
That waitress put
some kinda white powder

00:07:32.783 --> 00:07:34.575
in the young lad's javaccino!

00:07:34.658 --> 00:07:36.158
The poor sap
listened to his earphone

00:07:36.241 --> 00:07:38.283
while he gulped it
down none the wiser.

00:07:38.366 --> 00:07:40.533
Yeah. It was in his left ear!

00:07:42.366 --> 00:07:44.741
[PHOENIX]
He doesn't seem to be lying.

00:07:44.825 --> 00:07:46.533
[KUDO]
Don't stare at me like that!

00:07:46.616 --> 00:07:48.616
I know, I'm just
an inconvenience!

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:50.366
At home, at that restaurant.

00:07:50.450 --> 00:07:52.741
All I'm good for
is running errands!

00:07:52.825 --> 00:07:54.533
Oh, errands, you say?

00:07:54.616 --> 00:07:55.741
Sure's you're born.

00:07:55.825 --> 00:07:58.533
On that very day the
unlucky lad met his end.

00:07:58.616 --> 00:08:00.450
Did somebody ask
you to do something for them?

00:08:00.533 --> 00:08:03.366
Yeah. That pasty chef!

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:05.491
Excusez-moi!

00:08:05.575 --> 00:08:08.533
Call zee policemen,
s'il vous plait, pépé!

00:08:08.616 --> 00:08:09.866
Whole thing had me
feeling like a deer

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:11.200
in the headlights.

00:08:11.283 --> 00:08:13.491
But I ran outta there
just like he asked me to.

00:08:13.575 --> 00:08:15.741
I needed to find
a pay phone, ya see.

00:08:15.825 --> 00:08:17.950
[PHOENIX] Why didn't
you use your cell phone?

00:08:18.033 --> 00:08:20.158
I don't trust those
new-fangled thingies.

00:08:20.241 --> 00:08:22.158
What then?
Did you find one quickly?

00:08:22.241 --> 00:08:25.366
'Fraid not. I ran around
looking for ten minutes or so.

00:08:25.450 --> 00:08:26.700
That long?

00:08:26.783 --> 00:08:29.116
And Maggey was passed out,
so the chef was alone.

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:30.908
[KUDO] Gotta say,
that definitely ruined

00:08:30.991 --> 00:08:32.616
my javaccino time.

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:34.200
[MIA]
Your javaccino time?

00:08:34.283 --> 00:08:36.908
[KUDO] My daily routine is to
enjoy a nice cup of javaccino

00:08:36.991 --> 00:08:38.991
at 2 PM sharp every day.

00:08:39.075 --> 00:08:40.658
That chef's got no sense.

00:08:40.741 --> 00:08:42.075
If you're carryin'
around that kinda debt,

00:08:42.158 --> 00:08:44.033
you should value your regulars!

00:08:44.116 --> 00:08:47.116
[PHOENIX] Wait. You know
about Armstrong's debt?

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:49.575
Sure do. And I recently
heard he let it blow up

00:08:49.658 --> 00:08:51.741
to 500,000 smackerooneys.

00:08:51.825 --> 00:08:53.033
Five hundred grand?!

00:08:53.116 --> 00:08:54.575
[KUDO] And then he
wants to cry about it

00:08:54.658 --> 00:08:56.366
bein' "society's fault."

00:08:56.450 --> 00:08:58.408
[PHOENIX] It's obviously
his cooking skills.

00:08:58.491 --> 00:09:00.325
[KUDO] Well, he borrowed
from the Tiger,

00:09:00.408 --> 00:09:02.075
so he shoulda seen this coming.

00:09:02.158 --> 00:09:03.158
That name again.

00:09:03.241 --> 00:09:04.616
[KUDO]
If you're in dire straits,

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:07.700
don't make the mistake of
goin' to the Tender Lender.

00:09:07.783 --> 00:09:09.158
You don't say.

00:09:09.241 --> 00:09:10.950
Is that this "Tiger's" business?

00:09:11.033 --> 00:09:12.200
That it is.

00:09:12.283 --> 00:09:14.825
But make no mistake--
he's just a loan shark.

00:09:14.908 --> 00:09:16.366
[MIA]
Thank you very much.

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:18.366
--I appreciate your help.
--[yells]

00:09:21.116 --> 00:09:22.408
Well, sir.

00:09:22.491 --> 00:09:24.866
Can you tell us where to
find this "Tender Lender?"

00:09:29.533 --> 00:09:31.200
[VIOLA]
You're here to discuss a loan.

00:09:31.283 --> 00:09:32.200
Is that right?

00:09:32.283 --> 00:09:33.366
Yes, we are.

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:35.575
The office manager
is away at the moment.

00:09:35.658 --> 00:09:37.866
So I hope you don't
mind waiting a bit.

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:39.033
[giggles]

00:09:40.950 --> 00:09:44.283
[PHOENIX] Yeah. That's
who we saw at Très Bien earlier.

00:09:44.366 --> 00:09:45.908
[clattering]

00:09:45.991 --> 00:09:46.991
[PHOENIX]
Hmm?

00:09:51.783 --> 00:09:54.158
[PHOENIX]
Maya! What are you doing?

00:09:54.241 --> 00:09:57.033
This is our
only chance! Come on.

00:09:57.116 --> 00:10:00.658
How are we gonna find any clues
if we don't start looking?

00:10:00.741 --> 00:10:02.366
Is this a good idea?

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:04.991
So much junk.
Where do we start?

00:10:06.325 --> 00:10:07.533
[PHOENIX]
Hold on.

00:10:07.616 --> 00:10:09.950
That the CD Maggey
told us about?

00:10:10.033 --> 00:10:13.408
[MAGGEY] No, it said
"MC"-something on it in marker.

00:10:13.491 --> 00:10:14.700
[PHOENIX]
Hmm.

00:10:18.866 --> 00:10:19.783
What's that?

00:10:19.866 --> 00:10:20.950
This appears
to be a work invoice

00:10:21.033 --> 00:10:22.741
from a car body shop.

00:10:22.825 --> 00:10:25.116
Whoa, that is a lot of money!
That's crazy!

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:27.825
[MAYA] The car's registered
to the Cadaverini Group.

00:10:27.908 --> 00:10:29.325
[PHOENIX]
Cadaverini?

00:10:29.408 --> 00:10:31.408
Hey, I noticed this earlier.

00:10:31.491 --> 00:10:33.116
Don't you think this
suit looks a lot like

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:34.700
the one you always wear?

00:10:34.783 --> 00:10:37.700
[PHOENIX]
Yeah. Hm? What the heck?

00:10:37.783 --> 00:10:39.200
[MAYA]
A badge like yours.

00:10:39.283 --> 00:10:41.950
[PHOENIX] But it's cardboard!
And nobody noticed?

00:10:42.033 --> 00:10:44.616
[TIGRE]
Hey! What's goin' on?!

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:46.908
How come you two is
snoopin' around my office?!

00:10:46.991 --> 00:10:48.241
Huh?!

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:52.575
Guess you figured
it out, didja tough guy?

00:10:52.658 --> 00:10:53.866
The Big City Tiger?

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:56.658
I didn' expect the
genuine article to show up.

00:10:56.741 --> 00:10:58.033
So you're the imposter?

00:10:58.116 --> 00:10:59.158
Say what?!

00:10:59.241 --> 00:11:00.491
[MAYA whimpers]

00:11:00.575 --> 00:11:02.033
Just calm down.

00:11:02.116 --> 00:11:04.075
[TIGRE] Yeah? How'm I s'posed
ta be calm when there's ash

00:11:04.158 --> 00:11:06.200
all over my Persian rug?

00:11:06.283 --> 00:11:07.366
Was it you?!

00:11:07.450 --> 00:11:08.741
No, I had nothing
to do with it, I swear!

00:11:08.825 --> 00:11:09.950
Listen, boul.

00:11:10.033 --> 00:11:12.158
I'm gonna pummel you
flatter than a pancake,

00:11:12.241 --> 00:11:14.366
then use youse as my new rug!

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:15.491
[MAYA whines]

00:11:15.575 --> 00:11:17.116
[VIOLA]
I'm sorry.

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:18.658
[TIGRE gasps]

00:11:18.741 --> 00:11:20.783
Look. I accidentally
knocked over

00:11:20.866 --> 00:11:22.741
the ashtray earlier.

00:11:22.825 --> 00:11:23.950
[TIGRE growls]

00:11:24.033 --> 00:11:25.991
[PHOENIX]
Oh, man. What am I gonna do?

00:11:26.075 --> 00:11:28.825
Now he's gonna
pancake her instead.

00:11:28.908 --> 00:11:30.408
It's okay,
I'm just glad you didn't

00:11:30.491 --> 00:11:32.783
hurt yourself doin' it.

00:11:32.866 --> 00:11:36.033
You know I could never
get angry at you, Violetta.

00:11:36.116 --> 00:11:37.533
[PHOENIX]
What happened to the pancaking?

00:11:37.616 --> 00:11:39.450
Huh? What was that?

00:11:39.533 --> 00:11:40.575
[PHOENIX]
Nothing!

00:11:40.658 --> 00:11:43.241
Well... Don Tigre
and I are lovers.

00:11:43.325 --> 00:11:44.700
He's very tender with me.

00:11:44.783 --> 00:11:46.283
Did you call him Don Tigre?

00:11:46.366 --> 00:11:48.200
Yeah! We're
cuckoo for each other!

00:11:48.283 --> 00:11:49.366
Got it?

00:11:49.450 --> 00:11:50.825
[MAYA whimpers]

00:11:50.908 --> 00:11:53.658
As a matter of fact, I owe
this incredible man my life.

00:11:53.741 --> 00:11:57.491
You see, I came awfully
close to dying recently.

00:11:57.575 --> 00:11:58.825
[giggles

00:11:58.908 --> 00:12:00.200
You almost died?

00:12:00.283 --> 00:12:03.241
Yes, but I was saved by
my knight in shining armor.

00:12:03.325 --> 00:12:05.366
He gave up everything for me.

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:06.533
[giggles]

00:12:06.616 --> 00:12:10.116
I'm so happy now. Don Tigre.

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:12.491
I'd do anythin'
for youse, dollface.

00:12:12.575 --> 00:12:13.575
[BOTH groan]

00:12:13.658 --> 00:12:14.908
What in the hell
are youse two deadbeats

00:12:14.991 --> 00:12:15.950
still doin' here?!

00:12:16.033 --> 00:12:17.783
Make like some eggs,
and scramble!

00:12:17.866 --> 00:12:19.200
[BOTH yell]

00:12:19.283 --> 00:12:20.700
[MAYA, PHOENIX]
Yes, sir!

00:12:20.783 --> 00:12:22.283
[GUMSHOE]
The Tender Lender?

00:12:22.366 --> 00:12:24.991
You might as well kiss your
keister goodbye, cupcake.

00:12:25.075 --> 00:12:26.408
I didn't borrow money.

00:12:26.491 --> 00:12:29.658
Even for a loan shark,
that operation is super fishy.

00:12:29.741 --> 00:12:31.866
And they've had some
sort of trouble lately.

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:33.366
I hear they've been
extra heavy-handed

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:34.950
on calling in their debts.

00:12:35.033 --> 00:12:37.158
So, uh... Do you
know who the gloomy lady

00:12:37.241 --> 00:12:39.158
we met at the office
could've been?

00:12:39.241 --> 00:12:41.158
Yeah. Viola Cadaverini.

00:12:41.241 --> 00:12:42.575
Wait a second.

00:12:42.658 --> 00:12:45.075
That was the name
I saw on the invoice!

00:12:45.158 --> 00:12:46.825
[GUMSHOE] She's the
only living granddaughter

00:12:46.908 --> 00:12:48.991
of Bruto Cadaverini.

00:12:49.075 --> 00:12:50.908
[PHOENIX]
Should I know who that guy is?

00:12:50.991 --> 00:12:53.325
[GUMSHOE] Head of the
Cadaverini crime family.

00:12:53.408 --> 00:12:56.158
Controls all the black
market cash in the city.

00:12:56.241 --> 00:12:59.616
He's got the Tiger by his tail,
and his you-know-whats.

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:00.991
He sounds scary.

00:13:01.075 --> 00:13:03.241
I'm glad we ran into her
instead of her grandfather.

00:13:03.325 --> 00:13:04.825
He's about
as tough as they come,

00:13:04.908 --> 00:13:06.658
but he sure has one
heck of a soft spot

00:13:06.741 --> 00:13:08.116
for that little girl of his.

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:09.950
Hey. Speaking of the Tiger,

00:13:10.033 --> 00:13:12.616
the victim borrowed some
scratch from him, too.

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:13.783
How much we talkin'?

00:13:13.866 --> 00:13:15.241
[GUMSHOE]
It was around a hundred grand.

00:13:15.325 --> 00:13:16.491
[gasps]

00:13:16.575 --> 00:13:18.241
Apparently, he was
a big-time gambler

00:13:18.325 --> 00:13:19.991
and that's where
all the money went.

00:13:20.075 --> 00:13:21.450
Stupid, but kinda gutsy.

00:13:21.533 --> 00:13:23.491
Wait, didn't he
win 500,000 big ones

00:13:23.575 --> 00:13:24.991
in the lottery that day?

00:13:25.075 --> 00:13:27.408
Five hundred grand! I won!

00:13:27.491 --> 00:13:29.741
Some guys really
do have all the luck.

00:13:29.825 --> 00:13:32.825
[PHOENIX] But... What was he
planning to do if he didn't win?

00:13:32.908 --> 00:13:35.241
He'd racked up
some serious debt.

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:38.241
[GUMSHOE] Well, according
to his coworkers,

00:13:38.325 --> 00:13:41.366
he said he was gonna use his
skills to pay those bills.

00:13:41.450 --> 00:13:42.533
[PHOENIX]
What do you mean?

00:13:42.616 --> 00:13:43.991
It seems that the
victim had programmed

00:13:44.075 --> 00:13:45.825
a nasty computer virus.

00:13:45.908 --> 00:13:47.241
What was he gonna do with it?

00:13:47.325 --> 00:13:49.325
If you can create one
with enough wallop to it,

00:13:49.408 --> 00:13:51.033
that sucker can
fetch you millions

00:13:51.116 --> 00:13:52.491
on the black market, easily.

00:13:52.575 --> 00:13:53.908
Now we're talkin'!

00:13:53.991 --> 00:13:56.700
Our boy was top of his
game, as far as programmers go.

00:13:56.783 --> 00:13:59.366
[PHOENIX] I've never been
savvy with computers myself.

00:13:59.450 --> 00:14:01.200
[GUMSHOE] I think
the virus he had written

00:14:01.283 --> 00:14:04.700
was called MC-something.

00:14:04.783 --> 00:14:06.908
Oh. Was it MC Pipe wrench?

00:14:06.991 --> 00:14:08.575
It was MC Bomber, wasn't it?

00:14:08.658 --> 00:14:09.783
Yeah, you're right.

00:14:09.866 --> 00:14:11.491
It was MC Bomber!

00:14:11.575 --> 00:14:13.075
[PHOENIX]
So that CD actually contained

00:14:13.158 --> 00:14:15.825
the virus that Glen Elg wrote.

00:14:15.908 --> 00:14:17.450
Dunno if this'll help ya,

00:14:17.533 --> 00:14:19.408
but it looks like the victim
was planning to meet up

00:14:19.491 --> 00:14:22.158
with somebody the day
he kicked his oxygen habit.

00:14:22.241 --> 00:14:23.783
Can you tell me who it was?

00:14:23.866 --> 00:14:25.950
[GUMSHOE] Sorry, but
I couldn't figure that out.

00:14:26.033 --> 00:14:28.366
Aw, man.
I'm sure you tried hard.

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:31.033
Oh, yeah. Hey, kid.

00:14:31.116 --> 00:14:32.658
There's something
else I had for ya.

00:14:32.741 --> 00:14:34.283
Ooh! Wonder what it is!

00:14:34.366 --> 00:14:35.991
Hang on. Well, actually.

00:14:36.075 --> 00:14:37.283
It's for Maggey!

00:14:37.366 --> 00:14:38.783
[PHOENIX, MAYA]
Huh?

00:14:38.866 --> 00:14:41.116
[MAYA]
A lunch box?

00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:43.825
Got up early this
morning to make it for her.

00:14:43.908 --> 00:14:45.158
I've been worried
because I could tell

00:14:45.241 --> 00:14:46.825
she's lost a lot of weight.

00:14:46.908 --> 00:14:48.283
That's a lot of weenies.

00:14:48.366 --> 00:14:49.533
Good work.

00:14:49.616 --> 00:14:51.366
I could eat a buttload
of these little guys.

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:53.658
So please, be a pal
and give this to her.

00:14:53.741 --> 00:14:56.241
Sure! Of course, pal!

00:14:56.325 --> 00:14:57.700
[TIGRE]
No problem!

00:14:57.783 --> 00:15:01.408
Yeah, be right there!
I'm just about to head that way!

00:15:01.491 --> 00:15:03.991
Aw, boss, you're
killing me with that joke!

00:15:04.075 --> 00:15:07.325
I'm dead! In stitches over here!

00:15:07.408 --> 00:15:10.325
Yeah, five minutes, tops.

00:15:10.408 --> 00:15:13.450
[snarls]
Damn it all!

00:15:13.533 --> 00:15:16.075
This is that
gloomy bitch's fault!

00:15:16.158 --> 00:15:17.450
[gasps]

00:15:19.658 --> 00:15:21.075
Wow! Weenies!

00:15:21.158 --> 00:15:24.741
They're my faves! Thank you.
Did you make this for me?

00:15:24.825 --> 00:15:26.408
Nah, it was all Gumshoe.

00:15:26.491 --> 00:15:28.116
So these are
Dick's weenies, huh?

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:29.741
He's been worried
half to death about you

00:15:29.825 --> 00:15:32.033
and wanted to make sure you
were getting enough to eat.

00:15:32.116 --> 00:15:33.075
[MAGGEY groans]

00:15:33.158 --> 00:15:34.241
Y'okay?

00:15:34.325 --> 00:15:36.658
Well, no. I can't
really eat this crap.

00:15:36.741 --> 00:15:38.241
You were so excited to get 'em.

00:15:38.325 --> 00:15:40.283
Why don't you take them, Maya?

00:15:40.366 --> 00:15:41.658
Are you sure?

00:15:41.741 --> 00:15:43.408
[MAGGEY]
Hmm.

00:15:43.491 --> 00:15:45.533
[TIGRE]
I'm headin' out, baby!

00:15:45.616 --> 00:15:46.575
See ya later.

00:15:46.658 --> 00:15:48.283
Please be careful.

00:15:52.991 --> 00:15:54.741
[VIOLA]
Don Tigre...

00:15:54.825 --> 00:15:59.700
[MAYA snarfing, gulping]

00:15:59.783 --> 00:16:01.158
I'm glad you're here Mr. Wright,

00:16:01.241 --> 00:16:02.241
because there's
something that

00:16:02.325 --> 00:16:04.200
I really wanted to
talk to you about.

00:16:04.283 --> 00:16:05.450
Yes, what?

00:16:05.533 --> 00:16:08.741
Well, it's concerning
the old man's testimony.

00:16:08.825 --> 00:16:10.283
At the time
I took the coffee over to

00:16:10.366 --> 00:16:12.950
the victim's table,
there was another customer

00:16:13.033 --> 00:16:14.991
inside the restaurant with us.

00:16:15.075 --> 00:16:17.533
Wait, do you mean
somebody other than the old man?

00:16:17.616 --> 00:16:19.200
Yeah. I do.

00:16:19.283 --> 00:16:21.991
There was a strange
woman there, too.

00:16:22.075 --> 00:16:23.033
[gasps]

00:16:23.116 --> 00:16:25.158
She had some
bandages on her head.

00:16:25.241 --> 00:16:26.158
And she was all like...

00:16:26.241 --> 00:16:27.158
[VIOLA's giggle]

00:16:27.241 --> 00:16:28.825
It was a really creepy laugh.

00:16:28.908 --> 00:16:30.158
Hey, isn't that...?

00:16:30.241 --> 00:16:31.991
She was present. You're sure?

00:16:32.075 --> 00:16:34.033
Definitely!

00:16:34.116 --> 00:16:37.033
Was she around because
she was involved somehow?

00:16:38.575 --> 00:16:40.825
I'm sorry, the
manager's out right now.

00:16:40.908 --> 00:16:42.158
[sighs]

00:16:42.241 --> 00:16:45.575
Viola. We're actually
here to ask you something.

00:16:49.866 --> 00:16:52.366
[VIOLA] There was a woman
with bandages on her head?

00:16:52.450 --> 00:16:54.158
Yes. And she laughed like this.

00:16:54.241 --> 00:16:55.158
[VIOLA's giggle]

00:16:55.241 --> 00:16:56.200
So...

00:16:56.283 --> 00:16:58.408
Huh. I have no clue
who it could be.

00:16:58.491 --> 00:17:00.075
[giggles]

00:17:00.158 --> 00:17:01.908
Uh... Seriously?

00:17:01.991 --> 00:17:03.450
[MAYA]
Hmm...?

00:17:03.533 --> 00:17:05.575
May I ask about your bandages?

00:17:07.075 --> 00:17:09.533
[MAYA] Oh, yeah! You
said you nearly died.

00:17:09.616 --> 00:17:11.450
It was a car accident.

00:17:11.533 --> 00:17:14.283
Four months ago, a motorbike
ran out in front of my car,

00:17:14.366 --> 00:17:15.616
and we collided.

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:22.408
Then, I had to undergo
a complicated surgery.

00:17:22.491 --> 00:17:24.950
The medical bills
were quite expensive.

00:17:25.033 --> 00:17:27.991
Thankfully, Don Tigre
was able to save me.

00:17:28.075 --> 00:17:29.366
How'd he do that?

00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:32.200
He paid for all
my hospital expenses.

00:17:32.283 --> 00:17:34.616
He said it was out of love.

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:37.158
That's so noble.

00:17:37.241 --> 00:17:39.575
But do you really
believe that's the truth?

00:17:39.658 --> 00:17:40.991
[VIOLA gasps]

00:17:45.325 --> 00:17:47.158
[PHOENIX]
I apologize for snooping.

00:17:47.241 --> 00:17:49.658
But this is the
repair bill for a car.

00:17:49.741 --> 00:17:52.825
The vehicle's registered
to the Cadaverini Group.

00:17:52.908 --> 00:17:54.325
[VIOLA grunts]

00:17:54.408 --> 00:17:57.408
Four months ago, the person
who caused your accident...

00:17:57.491 --> 00:17:58.991
...was Don Tigre himself.

00:17:59.075 --> 00:18:01.283
[gasps]

00:18:01.366 --> 00:18:02.325
[PHOENIX]
Just look at his scooter.

00:18:02.408 --> 00:18:04.325
It's practically falling apart.

00:18:05.408 --> 00:18:08.408
[PHOENIX] Deep down.
You know this is the truth.

00:18:08.491 --> 00:18:11.158
No, sir. He was
being honest with me.

00:18:11.241 --> 00:18:13.200
I love you, Violetta.

00:18:13.283 --> 00:18:15.241
And that's all there is to it.

00:18:15.325 --> 00:18:16.866
[chuckles]

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:18.116
Can't you see?

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:20.200
That's why he stepped
in and saved my life.

00:18:20.283 --> 00:18:22.325
He spent all his money on me.

00:18:22.408 --> 00:18:24.366
I heard something
about your grandfather.

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:27.033
He controls the
black loan market.

00:18:27.116 --> 00:18:29.450
Of course,
Tigre can't anger him.

00:18:29.533 --> 00:18:31.866
And I heard that you,
his granddaughter,

00:18:31.950 --> 00:18:34.491
mean everything to him.

00:18:34.575 --> 00:18:37.366
If you weren't Bruto
Cadaverini's granddaughter,

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:39.825
would Tigre have
paid for your expenses?

00:18:41.241 --> 00:18:42.741
[VIOLA sobs]

00:18:42.825 --> 00:18:44.241
Hey, take it easy, Nick.

00:18:44.325 --> 00:18:45.575
I apologize, ma'am.

00:18:45.658 --> 00:18:48.075
But a person's freedom
is on the line here.

00:18:48.158 --> 00:18:50.325
Please tell us what you believe.

00:18:50.408 --> 00:18:51.825
[VIOLA whimpers]

00:18:51.908 --> 00:18:54.825
[TIGRE] This is that
gloomy bitch's fault!

00:18:59.533 --> 00:19:04.033
[VIOLA] You're right.
It's because of who I am.

00:19:04.116 --> 00:19:07.533
My operation was pretty cheap.

00:19:07.616 --> 00:19:09.033
Wait. Hold on.

00:19:09.116 --> 00:19:11.700
But didn't you say it
was super expensive?

00:19:11.783 --> 00:19:13.200
A million dollars.

00:19:13.283 --> 00:19:14.408
Eh?!

00:19:14.491 --> 00:19:15.783
The majority
of that money was

00:19:15.866 --> 00:19:18.908
for "compensation," though.
Punishment.

00:19:18.991 --> 00:19:21.491
[PHOENIX] Tigre had
to pay for the accident.

00:19:21.575 --> 00:19:23.700
The pieces are
falling into place.

00:19:24.991 --> 00:19:27.408
[VIOLA]
I wanted it to be real.

00:19:27.491 --> 00:19:29.575
I wanted to believe
that he loved me.

00:19:29.658 --> 00:19:32.533
That it wasn't because
of my grandfather.

00:19:32.616 --> 00:19:34.616
I tried to convince myself.

00:19:34.700 --> 00:19:38.575
Even though it was a lie.
I just wanted it so badly.

00:19:38.658 --> 00:19:39.825
Viola...

00:19:39.908 --> 00:19:42.741
And so I did every
possible thing I could.

00:19:42.825 --> 00:19:45.741
To help Don get back
on his feet again.

00:19:45.825 --> 00:19:47.866
I... I'm sorry.

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:49.866
[sobs]

00:19:58.533 --> 00:19:59.783
Where are you going?

00:20:06.491 --> 00:20:09.575
Take these. They may help you.

00:20:09.658 --> 00:20:12.158
What's in here?

00:20:12.241 --> 00:20:16.533
Don Tigre. Watch your back.

00:20:16.616 --> 00:20:17.908
Huh?

00:20:17.991 --> 00:20:19.325
[PHOENIX gasps]

00:20:23.241 --> 00:20:25.741
That was such
a depressing story.

00:20:25.825 --> 00:20:28.908
[PHOENIX]
Look. Viola's medical records.

00:20:28.991 --> 00:20:31.825
[MAYA]
Why did she give those to us?

00:20:31.908 --> 00:20:35.575
[VIOLA]
Don Tigre. Watch your back.

00:20:35.658 --> 00:20:37.908
Watch your back, huh?

00:20:37.991 --> 00:20:40.741
Maybe. Check the back?

00:20:40.825 --> 00:20:41.991
[PHOENIX]
Hmm.

00:20:42.075 --> 00:20:42.991
[gasps]

00:20:43.075 --> 00:20:44.533
--There it is.
--[engine putting]

00:20:44.616 --> 00:20:46.075
[MAYA]
Huh?

00:20:46.158 --> 00:20:49.700
[TIGRE]
Hey! You two punks again?

00:20:49.783 --> 00:20:52.158
Whatchu got, huh? Lemme see it.

00:20:52.241 --> 00:20:54.241
Uh, Nick, what are
we gonna do now?

00:20:54.325 --> 00:20:56.200
What'd that dumb broad give you?

00:20:56.283 --> 00:20:58.408
Just cuz her
grandpop's the boss,

00:20:58.491 --> 00:21:01.616
she thinks she's hot stuff.
Hand that over!

00:21:01.700 --> 00:21:03.866
Not a chance. You've no right!

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:06.366
Huh?! Youse wanna
play games wid me?!

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:07.366
[GUMSHOE]
Hold it!

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:08.366
[TIGRE grunts]

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:10.366
[MAYA shrieks]

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:11.408
[GUMSHOE growls]

00:21:11.491 --> 00:21:12.616
Detective Gumshoe?

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:13.616
[MAYA gasps]

00:21:13.700 --> 00:21:16.241
Huh? A detective?

00:21:16.325 --> 00:21:17.991
You ain't gonna stop me, copper!

00:21:18.075 --> 00:21:19.616
[yells]

00:21:21.450 --> 00:21:22.825
Leave this guy to me!

00:21:22.908 --> 00:21:24.116
[MAYA]
You sure you got this?

00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:25.491
Just get outta here!

00:21:25.575 --> 00:21:27.116
You gotta save Maggey!

00:21:27.200 --> 00:21:29.658
If you don't,
she'll be convicted.

00:21:29.741 --> 00:21:31.533
Count on us. Let's go.

00:21:31.616 --> 00:21:32.783
Yeah!

00:21:34.991 --> 00:21:38.033
[PHOENIX] There are two things
I consider inexcusable.

00:21:38.116 --> 00:21:40.700
Poisoning and betrayal.

00:21:40.783 --> 00:21:45.033
They're the cowardly acts,
and the most hurtful crimes.

00:21:45.116 --> 00:21:47.450
I'm going to settle
this in court tomorrow!

00:23:20.450 --> 00:23:22.283
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:23:22.366 --> 00:23:25.241
I'm getting closer to
the truth, I can feel it.

00:23:25.325 --> 00:23:27.533
The Tiger, who
pretended to be me.

00:23:27.616 --> 00:23:29.658
The bottle found at Très Bien.

00:23:29.741 --> 00:23:32.200
Mr. Armstrong's debt
to a loan shark.

00:23:32.283 --> 00:23:34.408
The truth behind MC Bomber.

00:23:34.491 --> 00:23:36.283
The other man Maggey saw.

00:23:36.366 --> 00:23:37.533
It must have been...

00:23:37.616 --> 00:23:38.908
Yes!

00:23:38.991 --> 00:23:41.158
Everything will be revealed
in the upcoming trial.

00:23:41.241 --> 00:23:43.866
Find the contradictions!
Believe in the truth!

00:23:43.950 --> 00:23:47.075
Next episode: "Recipe for
Turnabout -- Last Trial"!

00:23:47.158 --> 00:23:48.408
Take that!
